Analyze this {language} code for Domain-Driven Design (DDD) violations.

Source file:
{source}

Return a JSON array of violations:
{{
  "pattern": "anemic-domain-model|business-logic-in-service|ubiquitous-language-violation|aggregate-boundary-violation|missing-value-object",
  "class_or_method": "name",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "violation": "what DDD principle is broken",
  "suggestion": "how to fix with DDD patterns"
}}

Anemic domain model: entity/aggregate with only getters/setters and no behavior methods.
Business logic in service: service/controller containing domain rules (calculations, validations)
  that belong in the domain model.
Ubiquitous language violation: technical names (UserData, ProcessItem) for domain concepts
  that should use domain language.
Aggregate boundary: directly referencing internal entities of another aggregate.
Missing value object: primitive obsession where a Value Object would capture business rules
  (Money, Email, Address as raw strings/ints).

Return [] if no violations. Return ONLY the JSON array.
